    "https://conncoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/1736": {
      "title": "Deputy Chief Information Officer (Deputy CIO) / Acting Director of Enterprise Systems",
      "description": "Connecticut College Portal | Deputy Chief Information Officer (Deputy CIO) / Acting Director of Enterprise Systems Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Connecticut College Deputy Chief Information Officer (Deputy CIO) / Acting Director of Enterprise Systems Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Deputy Chief Information Officer (Deputy CIO) / Acting Director of Enterprise Systems Department Information Services - Office of VP -Group Pay Type Exempt Appointment Type (A) Continuing Full-Time Hours Per Week 37.5 Number of weeks 52 weeks per year other - # of weeks 52 Benefits Eligible Full Benefits Geographical Regional Qualifies for Relocation Reimbursement No Work Schedule Job Description General Scope of Duties General Scope of Duties The Deputy Chief Information Officer (Deputy CIO ) serves as the senior technology strategist and operational leader within Library & Information Technology at Connecticut College. Reporting directly to the Vice President for Information Services and Librarian of the College ( CIO ), the Deputy CIO is responsible for translating institutional strategy into technology execution, ensuring the operational resilience and scalability of the College’s technology infrastructure, and serving as the primary technology leadership partner to the VP. During an initial transitional period (12-14 months), this role will also serve as Acting Director of Enterprise Systems, providing direct oversight and stabilization leadership to the Enterprise Systems team while the College evaluates its long-term ERP modernization path. Following this initial period, the role transitions to broader strategic oversight while serving as the VP’s primary strategic partner for all infrastructure and enterprise systems initiatives. This position is in-person with potential to work remotely one day per week; In-person collaboration will be essential for key events and meetings. About Library & Information Technology at Connecticut College Library & Information Technology (L&IT) at Connecticut College is where librarians, technologists, archivists, media specialists, and everything in between come together as one team. We manage the systems that run the College, the network that connects it, the library that anchors it, and the research support that makes academic excellence possible. Whether someone needs help finding a rare archival document, troubleshooting a classroom projector five minutes before class, or thinking through the future of AI on a liberal arts campus, that’s us. And we don’t work in a bubble. Our staff regularly connect with colleagues at peer institutions through consortia like the Boston Library Consortium, the Oberlin Group, CLAC , and NERCOMP , because we believe the best ideas rarely stay inside one campus. Why You’ll Love It Here (And Why We’ll Love You) Our leadership philosophy is pretty simple: We hire naturally curious people, give them room to be brilliant, and then get out of their way. We treat belonging and inclusion as the foundation of our work, not a footnote. We value collaboration over control, and we believe that while the work is serious, we absolutely do not have to take ourselves too seriously. If you can work hard, lead with curiosity, tolerate the occasional Swedish-inspired coffee break (look up fika), and agree that laughter is a legitimate workplace requirement, you’ll fit right in. General Duties and Responsibilities Primary Duties and Responsibilities • Serve as the operational and strategic technology leader for Library & Information Technology, partnering closely with the VP to advance divisional and institutional priorities • Provide interim leadership and direct supervision to the Enterprise Systems team, ensuring continuity of operations, staff support, and forward progress on key systems initiatives during a transitional period • Provide direct supervision and professional development support to the Assistant Director of Network and Systems Infrastructure, Technical Lead for Enterprise Applications, and the Technical Lead for Web Applications, fostering a culture of accountability, collaboration, and continuous improvement • Ensure technology projects are scoped, resourced, prioritized, and delivered in alignment with institutional goals (in collaboration with L&IT Project Manager) • In collaboration with direct reports, Lead the development and implementation of a comprehensive technology roadmap, including cloud strategy, identity and access management, and systems integration • Partner with the Director of Information Security to ensure technology infrastructure decisions incorporate security, privacy, and compliance requirements from the outset • Collaborate with institutional stakeholders across academic affairs, finance, student life, and advancement to ensure technology services are responsive, equitable, and mission-aligned • Assess opportunities for infrastructure consolidation and modernization, including network upgrades, data center strategy, and disaster recovery planning • Serve as the technical expert for vendor evaluations and contract negotiations across all infrastructure and enterprise systems domains Secondary Duties and Responsibilities • Contribute to divisional budget planning, resource prioritization, and zero-based budget processes in alignment with the College’s financial sustainability goals • Support the VP in developing and presenting technology strategy to the President’s Cabinet, Board of Trustees, and other institutional governance bodies • Lead or co-lead vendor relationship management for major technology contracts and partnerships • In collaboration with library colleagues, advance the College’s AI@Conn initiative by identifying responsible, scalable, and pedagogically sound applications of generative AI across administrative and academic functions • Promote data governance, data stewardship, and institutional data literacy across the division and the broader College community • Contribute to policy development related to technology use, information security, accessibility, and digital equity • Represent Library & Information Technology in cross-divisional working groups, task forces, and committees Tertiary Duties and Responsibilities • Engage in professional development by participating in relevant conferences, workshops, and training, including EDUCAUSE , NERCOMP , CLAC , and peer consortium engagements • As appropriate, participate in the life of the College by attending campus events such as L&IT speakers and events, athletic games, gallery openings, arts performances, student exhibits, and other signature experiences • Other duties or responsibilities as may be assigned Education and Skills • Bachelor’s degree required; advanced degree strongly preferred • At least seven years of progressive leadership experience in higher education information technology, with demonstrated success managing complex, multi-functional technology environments • Demonstrated ability to lead through ambiguity, including navigating organizational change, evolving technology landscapes, and institutional decision-making processes that are still in formation • Experience leading or significantly contributing to large-scale enterprise systems initiatives; direct ERP implementation experience is valued but not required • Strong change management and business process improvement skills, with the ability to bridge functional units and technical teams • Strong project portfolio management skills with the ability to prioritize competing demands in a resource-constrained environment • Demonstrated commitment to fostering a culture of belonging and ensuring technology solutions are accessible and inclusive for all members of the campus community • Excellent communication, collaboration, and relationship-building skills across technical and non-technical audiences • Experience supervising and developing professional staff with varied technical backgrounds • Familiarity with cloud strategy, identity and access management, and information security frameworks • A service-oriented mindset with the ability to build trust and credibility across the campus community • Experience with or strong interest in the responsible implementation of generative AI in a higher education context Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands The physical demands and work environment described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. • Ability to remain in a stationary position for extended periods • Frequent movement within office and campus environments; ability to traverse campus and navigate multi-level buildings • Ability to lift and carry up to 25 pounds occasionally • Repetitive motions including typing, using a mouse, and handling documents • Ability to communicate effectively in person, by phone, and electronically • Visual and auditory ability to complete job-related tasks Driving Required No Salary Range $120,000 - $150,000 Note Connecticut College is committed to fair and competitive compensation. The final offer will reflect the candidate’s experience, education, and the institution’s pay structure to ensure internal equity. Applicant Credentialing Thorough applicant credentialing will be conducted on the selected candidate which will include criminal records check, DMV check and depending on the position psychological exam and pre-placement physical. Posting Detail Information Open Date Applications accepted through Open Until Filled No Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you eligible to work in the U.S.? Yes No Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa)? Yes No To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://conncoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/1084": {
      "title": "Substitute Early Childhood Paraeducator",
      "description": "Connecticut College Portal | Substitute Early Childhood Paraeducator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Connecticut College Substitute Early Childhood Paraeducator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Substitute Early Childhood Paraeducator Department Children's Program -Group Pay Type Non Exempt Appointment Type (A) On Call Hours Per Week 1 Number of weeks Other (Benefits Ineligible) other - # of weeks 52 Benefits Eligible No Benefits Geographical Regional Qualifies for Relocation Reimbursement No Work Schedule Job Description General Scope of Duties General Description of Responsibilities: 1. Duties in relationship to individual children or in groups help teacher in curriculum implementation of educational program help with daily record keeping and appropriate reporting help teacher evaluate children as appropriate help teacher with case management help teacher in planning future placements maintain safe and organized physical environment for children help in data collection for research projects as required 2. Duties in relationship to other staff assist in daily set-up of classroom aid in implementing the programs of the professional specialists communicate effectively with team members maintain regular communication with Program Director, Laboratory Coordinator and teachers attend staff meetings when appropriate maintain positive professional work environment attend in-service meetings as appropriate 3. Duties in relationship to parents maintain informal contact with parents participate in parent social and educational functions with other staff, conduct home visits when appropriate discuss child’s program with parent and teacher when appropriate participate in formal parent conferences when required by teacher 4. Duties in relationship to college students help teacher in guiding college student classroom participation when appropriate General Duties and Responsibilities Education and Skills Qualifications: High school degree required. Within four months of hire, the selected candidate must be designated as eligible to have unsupervised access to children in a child care center by the CT Commissioner of Early Childhood. Experience: One year working with preschool age children necessary Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Driving Required No Salary Range $15.69 Note Connecticut College is committed to fair and competitive compensation. The final offer will reflect the candidate’s experience, education, and the institution’s pay structure to ensure internal equity. Applicant Credentialing Thorough applicant credentialing will be conducted on the selected candidate which will include criminal records check, DMV check and depending on the position psychological exam and pre-placement physical. Posting Detail Information Open Date 10/01/2024 Applications accepted through Open Until Filled Yes Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree PHD * How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ * Are you eligible to work in the U.S.? Yes No To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
